Title: The Lamplighter
Credit: Written by
Author: Jason Lenz
Draft date: 2025-03-02

.ACT ONE - A STATION PLATFORM, NIGHT

! A bare platform. One bench. A departure board that has not changed in an hour.

! ELLA sits with a suitcase she has not opened. MARTIN stands apart, reading the board.

ELLA
You have checked it four times.

MARTIN
Five.

ELLA
It says the same thing every time.

MARTIN
(not turning round)
It says delayed. It does not say cancelled. There is a difference and I intend to hold them to it.

ELLA
Sit down, Martin.

! He does not sit down.

MARTIN
If I sit down it becomes an evening. Standing up, it is still a delay.

ELLA
Then stand. You will be standing when the last train goes without us.

! A tannoy crackles. Neither of them looks up.

MARTIN
That is not for us.

ELLA
It is never for us.

MARTIN
(finally sitting)
Tell me something I do not know.

ELLA
I sold the house.

! A long pause. The departure board flickers once and settles.

MARTIN
Which house.

ELLA
There is only one house.

MARTIN
There was only one house.

ELLA
Yes. That is what I said.

! The platform lights dim by half. Somewhere down the line, a train that is not theirs goes through without stopping.

~ And the lamps go out along the line

~ One by one by one

MARTIN
You could have asked me.

ELLA
I did ask you. In March. You said you would think about it.

MARTIN
I was thinking about it.

ELLA
For eleven months.

! He has no answer. He picks up her suitcase. It is lighter than he expected and that is the thing that finally lands.

MARTIN
There is nothing in this.

ELLA
No.

MARTIN
Ella. There is nothing in this.

ELLA
I know what is in my own case.

! The board changes. For the first time all night, it changes.

> BLACKOUT <

CUT TO:

.ACT ONE, SCENE TWO - THE SAME PLATFORM, LATER

! The bench is empty. The suitcase is still there.
